explanation:
Using the Simple Interest formula $SI = \frac{P \times r \times T}{100}$ with $T = 12$ years, the total amount is $A = P + SI = P(1 + \frac{3r}{25})$. Solving for $r$ in each case: 
(i) $2P \implies r = 8\frac{1}{3}\%$ (c); 
(ii) $\frac{5P}{4} \implies r = 2\frac{1}{12}\%$ (a); 
(iii) $\frac{3P}{2} \implies r = 4\frac{1}{6}\%$ (d); 
(iv) $\frac{7P}{4} \implies r = 6\frac{1}{4}\%$ (b). 
Thus, the correct mapping is i-c, ii-a, iii-d, iv-b.
